  "id": "COMPOUND:7313 - PROTEIN:3374",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a strong, indirect relationship between the compound DIETHYL (1R,2S,3R,4S)-5,6-BIS(4-HYDROXYPHENYL)-7-OXABICYCLO[2.2.1]HEPT-5-ENE-2,3-DICARBOXYLATE and Ornithine decarboxylase, inducible. This compound is identified as a target of multiple agents, including 4-(2-aminoethoxy)-N-(3-chloro-2-ethoxy-5-piperidin-1-ylphenyl)-3,5-dimethylbenzamide and (2Z,3E)-2,3'-biindole-2',3(1H,1'H)-dione 3-{O-[(3R)-3,4-dihydroxybutyl]oxime}, which in turn target Ornithine decarboxylase, inducible. The shared target of these agents, Cytochrome b-c1 complex subunit 6, mitochondrial, indicates that the compound may interact with mitochondrial proteins, potentially through a common pathway. The evidence suggests that the compound may modulate mitochondrial function, which could influence the activity of Ornithine decarboxylase, a key enzyme in polyamine synthesis. The indirect nature of the relationship highlights the importance of mitochondrial targets in the compound's mechanism of action, though the exact molecular interaction remains to be elucidated.",
